-- allium: 3
-- retro-skill.allium
--
-- Scope: The /retro skill (plugin/skills/retro/SKILL.md and its
--        references/filing.md): what an agent running it guarantees to the
--        next agent dispatched into the repo, and to the operator whose
--        session it reflects on. It looks for moments where the operator
--        corrected or steered the agent, then changes the agent-facing
--        context that would have saved the effort, or files a task for what
--        it must not change itself.
-- Includes: Retrospective (one per invocation) and its pipeline — look,
--           judge, act, report; Moment, one point of user feedback, and what
--           became of it; what counts as a moment; which surfaces reach the
--           next agent; the fix-or-file split and the done-path exception; the
--           two tags it files; the root cause that lies outside the repo; the
--           report and the return to the calling skill.
-- Excludes: where the skill sits in a wrap-up (wrap-up-skill.allium:
--           RunRetro) and what refuses a dirty tree
--           (mcp-task-tools.allium: WrapUpRefusesUnfinishedWork, which holds a
--           retro fix to the commit but cannot tell whether retro ran); that
--           a retro task sorts after planned subtasks (epics.allium:
--           AutoDispatchNextSubtask); how the skill's copy reaches an agent
--           (mcp-task-tools.allium: SkillCopyIsJustInTime); what task_create
--           and learning_record do (mcp-task-tools.allium: CreateTaskViaMcp;
--           learnings.allium: RecordLearningViaMcp); the knowledge base itself (learnings.allium);
--           the tools behind each step (task_search) — those are the
--           skill's mechanics, not what it promises.
--
-- Design decisions:
--   - The subject is feedback the operator actually gave. A stale spec is the
--     weed skill's job and a command that failed until the right invocation
--     was found is a tooling problem, so neither is a moment. Without that
--     bound the skill turns into an audit of documentation accuracy, and an
--     inaccurate sentence that cost the session nothing is filed as a chore.
--   - Nothing notable is a real answer. A skill that must find something
--     invents it.
--   - The agent that did the work has the context and a commit as its next
--     step, so a small, self-evident prose fix is cheap for it and a task is
--     not. A fix that needs a design judgement, or whose history the agent
--     does not know, is a task, because the next agent can ask the questions
--     this one cannot.
--   - A spec describes behaviour the code has. Retro may bring a spec up to
--     what this session implemented; a spec for behaviour the code lacks is a
--     design change and runs spec, tests, code with its own dispatch.
--   - On a done wrap-up nothing rebases or pushes, so a fix stays in a
--     worktree that is then removed. A task survives it. Retro therefore
--     files and never fixes there.
--   - Retro files bug and chore and nothing else. A speculative refactor or
--     an enhancement idea is a hypothetical, not a finding, and it
--     is not filed.
--   - A workaround in the repo's docs treats the symptom. When the cause is
--     the tool or environment running the agent, the defect stays open until
--     someone files it, and only the repo that owns it may be filed into
--     silently.

use "./core.allium" as core

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Enumerations
------------------------------------------------------------

-- The surfaces whose content reaches the next agent, and how
-- (SKILL.md, "What is worth changing").
enum ContextSurface {
    claude_md          -- loaded into every dispatch prompt
    spec               -- docs/specs/*.allium, the source of truth agents consult
    doc_page           -- docs/*.md, linked from CLAUDE.md, read on demand
    skill              -- plugin/skills/*/SKILL.md, the skill the next agent invokes
    knowledge_base     -- injected into the prompt (learnings.allium)
    verify_command     -- shown by task_search and run by the agent
}

-- What a moment led to.
enum Disposition { fixed | filed | flagged | recorded | dropped }

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Entities and Variants
------------------------------------------------------------

-- One run of the skill, at the end of one task's work.
entity Retrospective {
    -- Known from the invocation or from task_search's wrap_up_mode, else asked
    -- for before the retrospective starts (ActionIsKnownBeforeFixOrFile).
    action: core/WrapUpMode
    moments: Moment with retro = this
    stage: looking | judging | acting | reported

    transitions stage {
        looking -> judging
        judging -> acting
        acting -> reported
        terminal: reported
    }

    fixed_moments: moments where disposition = fixed
    filed_moments: moments where disposition = filed
    flagged_moments: moments where disposition = flagged
    is_nothing_notable: moments.count = 0
    -- Every moment has a disposition. True at once for a retrospective with
    -- no moments.
    all_judged: stage = acting and moments.all(m => m.disposition != null)
}

-- One point where the operator corrected or steered the agent, confirmed a
-- design choice among options the agent offered, or stated a convention that
-- is written down nowhere. It may have cost no time.
entity Moment {
    retro: Retrospective
    -- A concrete event in this session, quoted or described. Never a
    -- hypothetical.
    event: String
    surface: ContextSurface?
    -- Would a change to that surface have saved the operator the effort?
    next_agent_would_do_better: Boolean
    -- The cause lies in the tool or environment running the agent (the
    -- sandbox, dispatch itself, Claude Code) rather than in this repo.
    root_cause_outside_repo: Boolean
    -- The surface is one the agent may edit: CLAUDE.md, a docs page, a skill
    -- or a spec (a spec only for implemented behaviour, below).
    is_editable_surface: Boolean
    -- This session's work made the surface wrong, or the session proved it wrong.
    session_made_it_wrong: Boolean
    -- The correction is small and self-evident.
    is_small_and_evident: Boolean
    -- The fix needs a design judgement, or the inaccuracy predates the
    -- session and its history is unknown.
    needs_judgement: Boolean
    -- The fix would make a spec describe behaviour the code lacks.
    describes_unimplemented_behaviour: Boolean
    -- A concrete defect the agent could not fix within the task.
    is_unfixed_defect: Boolean
    -- The tool or environment root cause is owned by the repo this task is in.
    owned_by_this_repo: Boolean

    -- A reusable pitfall, convention or preference: a design or style choice
    -- the operator corrected or confirmed.
    is_reusable_convention: Boolean

    disposition: Disposition?
    -- Only bug or chore (OnlyBugAndChoreAreTags).
    tag: core/TaskTag?

    -- Fixable in place: an editable surface, made wrong or proved wrong this session,
    -- small and needing no judgement. A spec edit is allowed only for
    -- behaviour this session already implemented.
    is_fixable_in_place:
        next_agent_would_do_better
        and is_editable_surface
        and not is_reusable_convention
        and not is_unfixed_defect
        and not root_cause_outside_repo
        and session_made_it_wrong
        and is_small_and_evident
        and not needs_judgement
        and not describes_unimplemented_behaviour

    -- The cause lies in a tool or environment another repo owns.
    has_foreign_root_cause: root_cause_outside_repo and not owned_by_this_repo

    -- A moment retro may act on at all.
    is_admitted: next_agent_would_do_better
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Config
------------------------------------------------------------

config {
    -- What the skill says first.
    announcement: String = "I'm using the retro skill to run a session retrospective."
    -- The heading line the report starts with.
    report_heading: String = "## Session Retrospective"
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Rules
------------------------------------------------------------

-- == Step 1: look ==

rule StartRetro {
    when: RetroRequested(action?)

    ensures: Retrospective.created(
        action: action_or_asked(action),
        stage: looking
    )
    ensures: RetroAnnounced(text: config.announcement)

    @guidance
        -- Invoked by the /wrap-up skill after the action is settled and
        -- before its commit step (wrap-up-skill.allium: RunRetro holds the
        -- order); the operator may also run /retro or ask for a
        -- session retrospective. The invocation carries the action; when it
        -- does not, the action is read from wrap_up_mode in task_search, and
        -- when that does not say either, the agent asks
        -- (ActionIsKnownBeforeFixOrFile).
}

rule LookForMoments {
    when: MomentNoticed(retro, event)

    requires: retro.stage = looking

    ensures: Moment.created(
        retro: retro,
        event: event,
        surface: surface_of(event),
        next_agent_would_do_better: would_next_agent_do_better(event),
        root_cause_outside_repo: is_tool_or_environment_cause(event),
        is_editable_surface: is_editable(surface_of(event)),
        session_made_it_wrong: made_wrong_by_session(event),
        is_small_and_evident: is_small_fix(event),
        needs_judgement: needs_design_judgement(event),
        describes_unimplemented_behaviour: spec_would_outrun_code(event),
        is_unfixed_defect: is_defect_left_open(event),
        owned_by_this_repo: repo_owns_cause(event),
        is_reusable_convention: is_convention(event),
        disposition: null,
        tag: null
    )

    @guidance
        -- One Moment per point of operator feedback the agent notices.
}

rule LookingDone {
    when: LookingFinished(retro)

    requires: retro.stage = looking

    ensures: retro.stage = judging

    @guidance
        -- The subject is feedback the operator actually gave
        -- (OnlyOperatorFeedbackIsASubject): a code review comment that
        -- changed something the agent had written, a design choice the
        -- operator made, a correction to the agent's plan, a convention
        -- stated that is written down nowhere. A moment counts even if it
        -- cost no time, because a future agent would meet the same choice
        -- and might get it wrong (WhatCountsAsAMoment). A stale spec is the
        -- weed skill's, and a command that failed until the right invocation
        -- was found is a tooling problem; neither is a moment. Nothing
        -- notable is a real and common answer (NothingNotableIsAnAnswer).
}

-- == Step 2: judge ==

rule JudgeMoment {
    when: retro: Retrospective.stage transitions_to judging

    for moment in retro.moments:
        requires: moment.disposition = null

        ensures:
            if not moment.is_admitted:
                moment.disposition = dropped

    ensures: retro.stage = acting

    @guidance
        -- For each moment the agent asks whether a change to one of the
        -- surfaces that reach the next agent would have prevented it. The
        -- test is whether the next agent would do better, and each moment
        -- must trace to a concrete event of this session
        -- (MomentsTraceToTheSession). A true but harmless inaccuracy is not a
        -- moment. The agent also asks whether the root cause sits in the
        -- tool or environment running it — the sandbox, dispatch itself or
        -- Claude Code — and if so reads references/filing.md before it acts
        -- (RootCauseOutsideTheRepoIsNotClosedByAWorkaround).
}

-- == Step 3: act ==

rule FixInPlace {
    when: retro: Retrospective.stage transitions_to acting

    for moment in retro.moments:
        requires: moment.is_admitted
        requires: moment.disposition = null
        requires: moment.is_fixable_in_place
        requires: retro.action in {rebase, pr}

        ensures: moment.disposition = fixed
        ensures: ContextEdited(surface: moment.surface, event: moment.event)

    @guidance
        -- The agent edits the surface now, in its worktree, and the edit
        -- travels with the session's own commit
        -- (SmallDriftIsFixedNotFiled). A spec is edited only to describe
        -- behaviour this session already implemented
        -- (SpecEditsDescribeImplementedBehaviour).
}

rule FileInsteadOfFixing {
    when: retro: Retrospective.stage transitions_to acting

    for moment in retro.moments:
        requires: moment.is_admitted
        requires: moment.disposition = null
        requires: retro.action = done
            or not moment.is_fixable_in_place
            or moment.is_unfixed_defect
        requires: not moment.is_reusable_convention
        requires: not moment.has_foreign_root_cause

        ensures: moment.disposition = filed
        ensures: moment.tag = if moment.is_unfixed_defect: bug else: chore
        ensures: TaskFiled(
            tag: moment.tag,
            repo_path: this_repo(),
            epic_id: retro_task_epic(),
            title: names_the_change(moment),
            description: cold_readable(moment)
        )

    @guidance
        -- task_create, with tag bug for a concrete defect with observable
        -- wrong behaviour and chore for a context improvement that passed
        -- the worth-changing test but that the agent must not fix itself
        -- (OnlyBugAndChoreAreFiled, FeaturesAreNeverFiled). A moment is
        -- filed rather than fixed when the fix needs a design judgement, is
        -- not small, concerns an inaccuracy whose history the agent does not
        -- know, or would make a spec describe behaviour the code lacks —
        -- that is a spec, tests, code loop with its own dispatch
        -- (SpecEditsDescribeImplementedBehaviour) — and a concrete defect
        -- that could not be fixed in scope is filed as a bug. On a done
        -- wrap-up it is always filed (DoneWrapUpAlwaysFiles).
        --
        -- The title names the change; the description names this task and
        -- says what the next agent will hit if it stays unfixed. repo_path
        -- and epic_id are required and not inherited: the finding goes in
        -- the epic of the task that found it, or null when it stands alone
        -- (FilingIsDuplicateCheckedAndWrittenForAColdAgent).
}

rule FlagForeignRootCause {
    when: retro: Retrospective.stage transitions_to acting

    for moment in retro.moments:
        requires: moment.is_admitted
        requires: moment.disposition = null
        requires: moment.has_foreign_root_cause

        ensures: moment.disposition = flagged
        ensures: RootCauseFlagged(event: moment.event)

    @guidance
        -- A workaround in this repo's docs may be written first when it helps
        -- the next agent now, but it is not sufficient closure. When another
        -- repo owns the defect, nothing is filed on that repo's board: the
        -- agent names the root cause and the repo it thinks owns it in the
        -- report, so the operator can file it, and says plainly that it is
        -- still open (RootCauseOutsideTheRepoIsNotClosedByAWorkaround).
}

rule RecordLearning {
    when: retro: Retrospective.stage transitions_to acting

    for moment in retro.moments:
        requires: moment.is_admitted
        requires: moment.is_reusable_convention

        ensures: LearningRecorded(event: moment.event)
        ensures:
            if not moment.has_foreign_root_cause:
                moment.disposition = recorded

    @guidance
        -- A reusable pitfall, convention or preference — a design or style
        -- choice the operator corrected or confirmed — is recorded with
        -- learning_record at once, without waiting to be asked
        -- (LearningsAreRecordedWithoutBeingAsked). The learnings skill owns
        -- how. A convention whose root cause lies in another repo's tool is
        -- still recorded, but the moment is flagged, not recorded: the
        -- foreign root cause wins the disposition (FlagForeignRootCause,
        -- RootCauseOutsideTheRepoIsNotClosedByAWorkaround).
}

-- == Step 4: report ==

rule ActingDone {
    when: retro: Retrospective.all_judged

    requires: retro.stage = acting

    ensures: retro.stage = reported
    ensures: RetroReported(
        heading: config.report_heading,
        went_well: went_well(retro),
        corrected_or_steered: retro.moments,
        context_fixed: retro.fixed_moments,
        tasks_filed: retro.filed_moments,
        root_causes_flagged: retro.flagged_moments
    )
    ensures: CallerResumed()

    @guidance
        -- A short summary under "## Session Retrospective" with five lines:
        -- what went well, where the operator corrected or steered, what
        -- context was fixed and where (or none needed), which follow-up tasks
        -- were created (or none needed), and the root causes flagged
        -- elsewhere (or none) (ReportHasFiveLines). It is not the end of the
        -- session: retro is a sub-step, so the agent goes straight on to the
        -- calling skill's next instruction in the same turn
        -- (ResumesTheCallingSkill).
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Invariants
------------------------------------------------------------

-- A moment becomes a fix only on a path where the fix reaches the base
-- branch.
invariant DoneNeverFixes {
    for moment in Moments:
        moment.disposition = fixed implies moment.retro.action in {rebase, pr}
}

-- Retro files only bug and chore.
invariant OnlyBugAndChoreAreTags {
    for moment in Moments:
        moment.disposition = filed implies moment.tag in {bug, chore}
}

-- A tool or environment root cause owned by another repo is never filed onto
-- that repo's board by retro.
invariant ForeignRootCauseIsNeverFiled {
    for moment in Moments:
        moment.has_foreign_root_cause implies moment.disposition != filed
}

------------------------------------------------------------
-- Surfaces
------------------------------------------------------------

surface RetroInvocation {
    facing _: core/Operator

    provides:
        RetroRequested(action?)

    @guidance
        -- The wrap-up skill invokes retro as a sub-step with the action it is
        -- wrapping up with; the operator may run /retro directly or ask for a
        -- session retrospective. To finish a task the agent uses the wrap-up
        -- skill, never this one. The plugin skill is /dispatch:retro.
}

surface RetroSession {
    facing _: core/Operator

    context retro: Retrospective

    exposes:
        retro.fixed_moments
        retro.filed_moments
        retro.flagged_moments
        retro.is_nothing_notable

    provides:
        MomentNoticed(retro, event) when retro.stage = looking
        LookingFinished(retro) when retro.stage = looking

    @guarantee AnnouncesItself
        -- The skill says "I'm using the retro skill to run a session
        -- retrospective." at the start (StartRetro).

    @guarantee ActionIsKnownBeforeFixOrFile
        -- Fix-or-file depends on the wrap-up action, so the agent has it
        -- before it acts: from the invocation, else from wrap_up_mode in
        -- task_search, else by asking. Retro does not guess it (StartRetro).

    @guarantee OnlyOperatorFeedbackIsASubject
        -- The subject is feedback the operator actually gave. A stale spec is
        -- the weed skill's job and a command that failed until the right
        -- invocation was found is a tooling problem; neither is a moment
        -- (LookForMoments).

    @guarantee WhatCountsAsAMoment
        -- A moment is the operator correcting or steering the agent's
        -- approach, confirming a design choice among options the agent offered,
        -- or stating a convention written down nowhere: a code review comment
        -- that changed something the agent had written, a design choice the
        -- operator made, a correction to the agent's plan. It counts even if
        -- it cost no time, since a future agent would hit the same choice
        -- (LookForMoments).

    @guarantee NothingNotableIsAnAnswer
        -- "Nothing notable" is a real and common answer. The skill does not
        -- invent a finding, so a smooth session is not turned into busywork
        -- (LookForMoments, Retrospective.is_nothing_notable).

    @guarantee MomentsTraceToTheSession
        -- The admission test is whether the next agent would do better, not
        -- whether a sentence is inaccurate. Every moment traces to a concrete
        -- event of this session; a true but harmless inaccuracy is not a
        -- moment (JudgeMoment, Moment.is_admitted).

    @guarantee SmallDriftIsFixedNotFiled
        -- When the surface is agent-facing prose (CLAUDE.md, a docs page that
        -- is not a spec, or a skill), the session made it wrong or proved it
        -- wrong, and the correction is small and self-evident, the agent fixes
        -- it itself, now: it has the context and the next step is a commit.
        -- Retro does not forbid editing (FixInPlace, Moment.is_fixable_in_place).

    @guarantee SpecEditsDescribeImplementedBehaviour
        -- A spec is the agent's to edit only to describe behaviour this
        -- session already implemented. A fix that would make a spec describe
        -- behaviour the code lacks is filed: it is a spec, tests, code loop
        -- with its own dispatch (FixInPlace, FileInsteadOfFixing).

    @guarantee FileWhenTheFixIsNotTheAgentsToMake
        -- A moment whose fix needs a design judgement, is not small, or
        -- concerns a pre-existing inaccuracy whose history the agent does not
        -- know is filed with task_create, not fixed. So is a concrete defect
        -- the agent could not fix in scope, as a bug (FileInsteadOfFixing).

    @guarantee DoneWrapUpAlwaysFiles
        -- On a done wrap-up nothing rebases or pushes, so an edit would be
        -- stranded in the worktree. Retro files a task instead of fixing, for
        -- every moment it would otherwise fix or file (a root cause another
        -- repo owns is still flagged, not filed) (FileInsteadOfFixing, DoneNeverFixes).

    @guarantee OnlyBugAndChoreAreFiled
        -- Retro files bug for a concrete defect with observable wrong
        -- behaviour and chore for a context improvement that passed the
        -- worth-changing test and that it must not fix itself
        -- (FileInsteadOfFixing, OnlyBugAndChoreAreTags).

    @guarantee FeaturesAreNeverFiled
        -- Retro never files a feature. A speculative refactor or an
        -- enhancement idea is not a finding; "this invariant is enforced by
        -- convention, so the same omission could recur" is a hypothetical, not
        -- a defect (FileInsteadOfFixing, OnlyBugAndChoreAreTags).

    @guarantee FilingIsDuplicateCheckedAndWrittenForAColdAgent
        -- Before filing, task_search is searched for a task that already covers
        -- the finding. A finding that spans several files is one task, not one
        -- per file. The title names the change, the description names this task
        -- and says what the next agent will hit if it stays unfixed, and
        -- repo_path and epic_id are passed explicitly: the task's own epic, or
        -- null when it stands alone (FileInsteadOfFixing).

    @guarantee ZeroTasksIsTheNormalOutcome
        -- Filing several tasks means the agent is recording nits. Zero tasks
        -- is the normal outcome (FileInsteadOfFixing).

    @guarantee RootCauseOutsideTheRepoIsNotClosedByAWorkaround
        -- For each moment the agent asks whether the root cause sits in the
        -- tool or environment running it: the sandbox, dispatch itself or
        -- Claude Code. A workaround in the repo's docs is written first if it
        -- helps the next agent, but is not sufficient closure. A defect this
        -- task's own repo owns is filed with task_create; a defect another repo
        -- owns is not filed silently but flagged in the report, naming the root
        -- cause and the repo. Either way the report says the root cause is
        -- still open (FileInsteadOfFixing, FlagForeignRootCause,
        -- ForeignRootCauseIsNeverFiled).

    @guarantee LearningsAreRecordedWithoutBeingAsked
        -- A reusable pitfall, convention or preference the operator corrected
        -- or confirmed is recorded with learning_record right away, and the
        -- agent does not wait to be asked (RecordLearning).

    @guarantee ReportHasFiveLines
        -- The report is a short summary headed "## Session Retrospective" with
        -- five lines: what went well; what the operator corrected or steered
        -- the agent on; the context fixed in this session and where, or none
        -- needed; the follow-up tasks created, or none needed; and the
        -- root-cause issues flagged elsewhere, or none (ActingDone).

    @guarantee ResumesTheCallingSkill
        -- The report is not the end of the session. Retro runs as a sub-step of
        -- wrap-up, so the agent resumes the calling skill's next instruction in
        -- the same turn and does not stop at the report (ActingDone).

    @guarantee DetailLivesInTheFilingReference
        -- The tags, the duplicate check, the call details and the
        -- root-cause routing live in references/filing.md, which SKILL.md names
        -- at the branch that needs it, so an agent that files nothing never
        -- loads it (mcp-task-tools.allium: SkillCopyIsJustInTime).
}
